# Serena QA then ship (Staging-first — critical)

This rule is **mandatory** for every agent on `wix-shmspto`. It overrides “only commit/push when asked” and overrides any habit of going straight to production.

After a complete, shippable **application** change, run Serena QA.

If Serena fails: fix and re-run. Do not commit, deploy, or push.

If Serena passes (diagnostics clean, scoped to the task), do this **exact** order:

## 1. Commit (local only)

- Commit **only** the files for that change.
- Do **not** `git push` yet.

## 2. Staging deploy (required hard gate)

- From a **clean worktree of that commit SHA**, deploy to the **stable staging host** (never `--prod` yet).
  - Stone Hill → Vercel project `frontend`, then **alias** the deployment to `shmspto.vercel.app`.
    Prefer: `node scripts/deploy-staging.mjs --cwd <clean-worktree>`.
  - Pavilion marketing → `commons-site` (use that project’s stable review URL if one exists; otherwise Preview URL).
  - Pavilion demo/trial → `commons-pto-demo` / `commons-pto` as relevant.
- Never deploy from a dirty working tree.
- **Do not** give Rob ephemeral `frontend-xxxxx.vercel.app` links for Stone Hill review. Always:
  **https://shmspto.vercel.app**
- In the reply, paste that staging URL and say production + GitHub are waiting on his OK.

## 3. STOP — wait for Rob

**Hard stop.** Do not continue until Rob explicitly approves with clear go-ahead, for example: `looks good`, `ship it`, `promote`, `go live`, `prod`, `push`, or `OK`.

Until then:

- Do **not** `vercel --prod` / `vercel promote … --prod`.
- Do **not** `git push`.
- Do **not** treat “done” as production. Done means **staging is up at shmspto.vercel.app and the link was delivered**.

## 4. After Rob approves: production, then GitHub

1. Promote that same staging deployment to production, or `vercel --prod` from the **same clean worktree SHA**.
2. **Then** `git push` that commit to GitHub.
3. After a **Stone Hill** application ship: **default to also deploying Pavilion** (`commons-pto-demo` / `commons-pto`) from the same SHA. Pavilion must stay vanilla (no SHMS branding or school-specific copy). Skip only for clearly SHMS-only work or if Rob says skip.

## Exceptions

- **Rules / docs / memories only** (no application runtime): commit then push. Skip staging and production.
- **Staff-only** (Staff dashboard, `/staff`, `components/staff`, `app/api/staff`, staff permissions/roles with no public visitor UI change): after Serena QA, commit from a **clean worktree of that SHA** → **staging** (`node scripts/deploy-staging.mjs --cwd <worktree>`, alias `shmspto.vercel.app`) **and** **production** (`vercel --prod` or promote that same SHA) → then `git push`. **Do not wait** for Rob OK. Staging must stay current with prod so staff review hosts do not go stale. If the same commit also changes public pages, membership, checkout, or visitor copy, use full Staging-first instead (staging only, then wait for OK).
- Never include unrelated WIP, secrets, Budget/Plaid/terminal/spirit-wear/`tmp` unless they are the task.
- Never mix Stone Hill and Pavilion env (DATABASE_URL, Wix, Square, Stripe).

## Anti-patterns (forbidden)

- Commit → `vercel --prod` → push in one turn without staging + Rob OK.
- Pushing to GitHub before production promote when this was an application ship.
- Calling the task “shipped” or “live” when only staging exists.
- Asking Rob to review on a one-off `frontend-*.vercel.app` Preview URL.
- Skipping staging for public visitor changes by labeling them “staff-related.”
- Staff-only prod deploy that leaves `shmspto.vercel.app` on an older SHA.

## Staging URL (Stone Hill)

https://shmspto.vercel.app

Google / Wix OAuth redirect URIs must include this host (see `scripts/google-workspace-admin-setup.md`).
